    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting high-ceiling matchups against soft opposing rotations. **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with a 72.72 efficiency score, bolstered by an advantageous home park and a favorable pairing against Mitch Keller. **James Wood** (71.11) remains a primary focal point; despite a minor efficiency haircut due to the opponent's ability to control the run game, his 0.407 xwOBA and leadoff position make him our most potent weapon for accumulating counting stats. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (68.63) is in an excellent position to capitalize on a weak SP matchup, while **Brice Turang** (66.63) receives a notable bump\u2014not just from his spot in the lineup, but because Cecconi\u2019s slower delivery tempo significantly elevates the probability of a successful swipe, which is vital given our strategic emphasis on SB scarcity.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was sidelining **Alex Freeland**, who clocked in at 37.77. While his switch-hitting versatility is a asset, he fell just short of our 40.0 \"Zebra\" floor due to a bottom-third of the order placement and a daunting date with Drew Rasmussen, whose 3.36 xERA dictates a more conservative approach. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Corbin Carroll** (52.12); he is active, but his score is suppressed by a tough matchup against Detmers and a negative platoon split. With **Jose Caballero** also battling a difficult platoon disadvantage (52.17), we are keeping a close eye on these fringe starts to ensure we don't bleed away our limited game caps on marginal outcomes. Avoid overexposure to the lower end of our lineup today; maintain focus on the high-efficiency anchors like **Soderstrom**, **Wood**, and **Suzuki** to pace our 5x5 categories.",
